  #line-at(288.12pt, 199.32pt, "Abstract  ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.2pt, 224.76pt, "The use of a thin solid electrolyte layer on polyethylene (PE) separators has been explored as a potential strategy to mitigate ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 236.52pt, "the polysulfide shuttle effect in lithium-sulfur (Li-S) batteries, a phenomenon responsible for significantly reducing their ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 248.4pt, "lifespan. While some solid electrolytes, such as LAGP (Li")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(298.92pt, 249.24pt, "1+x")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.68pt, 248.4pt, "AlₓGe")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(330.84pt, 249.24pt, "2-x")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(338.16pt, 248.4pt, "(PO")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(353.52pt, 249.24pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(356.16pt, 248.4pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(359.28pt, 249.24pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(362.04pt, 248.4pt, "), have demonstrated the ability to effectively ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 260.4pt, "suppress the shuttle effect, their brittle ceramic nature limits their application, particularly in flexible electronics. Coating PE ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 272.16pt, "separators with LAGP nanofilms offers a promising solution by combining the mechanical flexibility and thinness of ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 284.16pt, "polymer separators with the electrochemical advantages of LAGP, due to its NASICON-like structure and high ionic ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 296.04pt, "conductivity. In this study, PE separators were coated with LAGP nanofilms using the ion sputtering technique and further ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 307.92pt, "modified with ferroic elements such as Ni and Co. The surface morphology of the coated separators was analyzed using ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 319.8pt, "scanning electron microscopy (SEM), and staircase voltammetry was employed to evaluate the electrochemical ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 331.68pt, "performance and modifications induced by the coatings. The results demonstrate that the use of PE separators with a thin ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 343.56pt, "LAGP layer significantly influences polysulfide diffusion and suppresses the shuttle effect, thereby reducing unwanted ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 355.44pt, "processes in Li-S batteries.  ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 379.32pt, "Keywords: Energy storage systems, ion beam sputtering")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0f4761"))
  #line-at(271.32pt, 395.04pt, "1.")
  #line-at(288.24pt, 395.04pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.2pt, 420.48pt, "Energy storage devices are currently a hot topic in the scientific community due to their significant impact on ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 434.88pt, "modern society. As renewable energy storage facilities become more efficient and widespread, as the demand ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 449.04pt, "for advanced energy storage devices is growing. Lithium-sulfur (Li-S) batteries, along with other innovative ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 463.44pt, "systems, such as sodium-ion (Na-ion) batteries, are considered promising electrochemical solutions for the ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 477.6pt, "future of energy storage [1]. Li-S batteries offer several advantages, including their high theoretical capacity, ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 491.88pt, "high energy density, and low costs. However, their extensive use is hindered by poor cyclability, mainly due ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 506.16pt, "to the \"shuttle effect\" [2]. The shuttle effect arises from the migration and deposition of polysulfides on the ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 520.44pt, "electrode surface, which reduces conductivity and prevents further cycling. ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 540.36pt, "Various strategies have been explored to reduce or suppress the shuttle effect, aiming to decrease polysulfide ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 554.64pt, "diffusion and increase battery lifespan. A recent approach proposes the use of solid electrolytes with superior ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 568.8pt, "ionic conductivity to suppress polysulfide migration by acting as an additional physical barrier [3]. In this ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 583.2pt, "work, we aim to improve this strategy by combining LISICON materials, commercially available flexible ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 597.36pt, "polyethylene (PE) separators, and metallic coatings for Li-S applications. This experiment not only provides ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 611.76pt, "valuable insights into the cyclability and lifetime of Li-S batteries but also serves as a preliminary study on the ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 625.92pt, "effectiveness of LISICON material used in thin film form.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0f4761"))
  #line-at(269.76pt, 651.48pt, "2.")
  #line-at(286.68pt, 651.48pt, "Methodology  ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.2pt, 677.04pt, "Polyethylene separators with a thickness of 12 µm (Nanografi) were coated using the ion sputtering technique ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 691.32pt, "at the Low Energy Ion Facility (LEIF) in the NPI infrastructure [CANAM]. LEIF is a versatile ion beam facility ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 705.6pt, "that provides high current (in the mA range) for sputtering high-purity targets in a vacuum environment, as ")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 719.88pt, "well as for material irradiation/implantation at high fluences with energies ranging from 1 to 35 keV. High-")
  #line-at(79.2pt, 734.16pt, "quality LISICON material, specifically LAGP Li")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(281.88pt, 735pt, "1+x")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.08pt, 734.16pt, "AlₓGe")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.4pt, 735pt, "2-x")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(326.04pt, 734.16pt, "(PO")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(342.72pt, 735pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.358pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(346.08pt, 734.16pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.53pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
